// JsonValueStateActor — regression fixture for BT-3546 (ADR 0124 §7 A1)
//
// A typed-no-default state field whose type is an ADR 0108 alias that
// expands to a union containing `Nil` — mirroring `stdlib/src/json.bt`'s
// `type JsonValue = Nil | Boolean | Integer | Float | String | List |
// Dictionary`. Declared locally (rather than referencing the real stdlib
// `JsonValue`) because `beamtalk test`'s fixture/test-file compilation does
// not yet pre-load same-package `stdlib/src` type aliases the way it
// pre-loads `ClassInfo` — a separate, pre-existing gap in the `test`
// pipeline (only `beamtalk build` extracts project-wide `AliasInfo` via
// `collect_project_protocol_and_alias_infos`) filed as a follow-up rather
// than fixed here; the alias-resolution behaviour under test is identical
// either way, since `AliasRegistry` treats same-file and same-package
// aliases through the same lookup.
//
// Before BT-3546, the definite-assignment predicate did not resolve
// aliases, so `LocalJsonValue` was (wrongly) reported non-nilable and this
// actor raised `UninitializedStateError` at spawn even though `Nil` is a
// member of the alias's expansion. Should spawn successfully and leave
// `value` unset (`nil`).

type LocalJsonValue = Nil | Boolean | Integer | Float | String | List | Dictionary

typed Actor subclass: JsonValueStateActor
  state: value :: LocalJsonValue
  state: count :: Integer = 0

  initialize -> Integer =>
    // Deliberately does NOT set self.value — LocalJsonValue expands to
    // include Nil, so nil is a legitimate value here.
    self.count := 1

  getValue -> LocalJsonValue => self.value

  getCount -> Integer => self.count
